<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#arabic-language">Glossary</a> · Term · language</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arabic language</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Arabic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arabic is a Semitic language that spread with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-peninsula">Arabian Peninsula</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> it became the language of administration, replacing Greek and Persian in government records. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> it became a major language of science, philosophy and literature, and it heavily influenced Persian after the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>.</p></div>
